                <pb facs="0105" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1925: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-24T11:00:00+08:00">October 24, 1939—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 24—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>935. Chairman of Municipal Council informs me that he visited the Chinese Mayor
                    yesterday afternoon accompanied by the Senior Consul and the Japanese Consul
                    General and that conversations will be reopened with a view to seeking a
                    settlement of the outside roads problem, the Mayor requesting the Chairman to
                    submit several alternative proposals for consideration.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking and Peiping, code text by air mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
